### Assert copied query values rather than reference identity

**Severity:** `medium`

The toolkit deliberately copies the host-owned query arguments before starting asynchronous work. The current test fails at `AreSame`: the values may be correct while the new object cannot be reference-equal to `args`.

**If left unchanged:** the regression suite fails before checking the returned snapshot. Preserve the copy boundary and compare its fields rather than changing production behavior to satisfy the assertion.

```suggestion
        Assert.IsNotNull(fallback.LastQuery);
        Assert.AreEqual(args.Query, fallback.LastQuery.Query);
        Assert.AreEqual(args.QueryId, fallback.LastQuery.QueryId);
        Assert.AreEqual(args.RequestedItemCount, fallback.LastQuery.RequestedItemCount);
        CollectionAssert.AreEqual(args.LanguageTags, fallback.LastQuery.LanguageTags);
```

The current upstream toolkit test project builds with analyzers enabled; its unmodified fallback suite passes12/13 and fails this identity assertion. The literal candidate passes13/13. The author's sample override now uses `FallbackQueryArgs`, so the earlier sample-signature suggestion is withdrawn. No sample-project rebuild, host implementation or interactive execution is claimed for this revision.
